<title>FINLAND: FINNISH END-APRIL STATE DEBT UP TO FIM 425.2 BLN.</title>
<headline>FINNISH END-APRIL STATE DEBT UP TO FIM 425.2 BLN.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-05-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Finnish state debt rose by</p>
<p>2.25 billion markka in April to 425.2 billion markka by the end</p>
<p>of the month, the State Treasury Office (STO) said on Friday.</p>
<p>STO gave the following figures:</p>
<p>STRUCTURE OF GOVERNMENT DEBT, 30-04-1997</p>
<p>					    MILL.FIM	 MONTHLY CHANGE</p>
<p> TREASURY BILLS			   43,658		     -163</p>
<p> SERIAL BONDS			    147,020		    4,010</p>
<p> HOUSING BONDS			    13,126			  0</p>
<p> YIELD BONDS				30,777			207</p>
<p> OTHER DOMESTIC CURRENCY DEBT	 18,307		     -345</p>
<p> FOREIGN CURRENCY DEBT		 177,403		   -1,793</p>
<p> MISCELLANEOUS			    -5,107			333</p>
<p> TOTAL				     425,184		    2,249</p>
<p>--Helsinki newsroom +358-9-680 50 245, news@reuters.fi</p>
</text>
